-- BIR: `a.decode s` inside a declaration whose `where` clause constrains
-- the type variable `a` is a `type_dispatch` (§4.1): `a` binds no value —
-- it is not a local, a top-level value, an exposed name or a prelude value
-- — and it names a variable of this declaration's own clause, so the
-- application dispatches on the TYPE and is not a field access on a value.
pub decode : String -> Result String a
    where a.decode : String -> Result String a
decode s = a.decode s
